      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 2, open the case when an authorized owner has issued work instructions following an absence and operating teams need a precise implementation record. Do not let an urgent message become the control. Assign a stable case key, record who submitted the request and when, and preserve the original instruction. If the sender cannot be authenticated through the normal path, pause and ask the named owner for a safe verification route.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 3, the intake record for prepare a return-to-work record handoff should capture approved return date, permitted schedule facts, named owner, action recipients, confirmation status, and review date. Make each field either sourced, explicitly unknown, or not applicable. Blank cells are dangerous because a later reviewer cannot tell whether a fact was checked, omitted, or unavailable. Link to the controlled source instead of duplicating sensitive material in the work queue.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 4, use this operating sequence: translate only the released instruction into task assignments, confirm recipient need-to-know, and preserve the owner’s source reference. Preparation, review, approval, execution, and verification need separate states with timestamps. A single “done” label hides whether an action was merely drafted, actually authorized, performed in the destination system, or checked afterward.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 5, assign permissions to the smallest practical role. A coordinator may collect evidence, compare approved fields, draft a neutral exception note, and route work. HR and qualified owners decide eligibility, accommodation, restrictions, and any change to employment terms. Named accounts, multifactor authentication, restricted exports, and periodic access review help keep the workflow observable.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 6, design the exception path around the awkward case: two instructions conflict, a required fact is missing, or a manager asks the coordinator to interpret medical information. Preserve both sources and describe the exact difference. Do not overwrite an earlier value, choose the more convenient instruction, or convert uncertainty into an assumed approval. State which action is paused, who can decide, and when the next review occurs.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 7, a useful escalation note is short but reproducible. It identifies the case, affected step, facts checked, conflicting or missing evidence, deadline, operational consequence, and one precise question. Avoid a long narrative that mixes observation with recommendation. The receiving owner should be able to answer without reopening every unrelated employee record.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 8, before release, test one normal case, one incomplete case, and one deliberately conflicting case with fictional or masked data. Ask a second reviewer to reconstruct the source, authority, proposed action, and stop reason. Repair the instruction when two careful reviewers reach different states from the same evidence; disagreement often reveals an undefined field or stale owner map.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 9, closure for prepare a return-to-work record handoff means more than sending a message. Confirm schedule and access actions against the approved instruction, record acknowledgments, and remove unnecessary working copies. If the destination cannot be checked, mark the limitation and keep the case open or conditionally closed under an owner-approved rule. Evidence of activity is not automatically evidence of the intended outcome.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 10, review performance through unauthorized disclosures, conflicting versions, missed actions, overdue owner questions, incorrect schedules, and later reversals. Publish counts with their denominators and show the oldest unresolved high-risk case. A fast average can conceal one serious exception, while a large completion count can conceal repeated rework. Separate coordinator timeliness from owner-response time and from destination-system reliability.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 11, privacy belongs in the workflow design. Never put diagnoses or supporting health documents in an operations tracker; use a restricted reference and the minimum actionable instruction. Set a retention period for temporary evidence, control download locations, and remove working copies when their purpose ends. A convenient spreadsheet must not quietly become a second employee-record system.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 12, a weekly review should sample closed cases, inspect every boundary breach, and look for recurring causes such as unclear instructions, missing access, stale templates, unavailable owners, or system defects. Correct the cause through its owner and then resample. Coaching a coordinator cannot repair a policy contradiction or broken integration.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 13, use a launch gate before this workflow enters production: the scope is documented, decision owners accept their roles, permissions are tested, examples cover exceptions, the escalation channel works, and closure evidence can be retrieved. Start with a limited population and require explicit approval before expanding to adjacent employee decisions or data.",
      "For a return-to-work handoff checkpoint 14, the practical result is a handoff that another reviewer can reproduce. For prepare a return-to-work record handoff, good administration keeps facts, authority, action, and outcome distinct. This guide is general operational information, not legal, tax, benefits, security, or employment advice; organizations should adapt it with qualified owners for their policies and jurisdictions."
